---
source: tests/cli.rs
expression: project.run(args)
---
Read a session as markdown. The default shows user messages, Claude's replies, subagent reports and one line per reply summarising its tool use (files edited, commands run). --deep adds tool calls, results and thinking. --outline prints one line per turn instead. Output is paged by --budget; the last line names the --from that continues where the page stopped.

Usage: claudegrep read [OPTIONS] <SESSION>

Arguments:
  <SESSION>
          Session id (a unique prefix is enough) or its number from `list`

Options:
      --outline
          One line per turn instead of the content: the session's table of contents

      --deep
          Also show tool calls, tool results and thinking

      --from <POSITION>
          Start reading here: TURN.PART from search, or the position printed at the end of a page

      --turn <N>
          Show turn N with --context turns either side

      --context <K>
          Turns either side of --turn [config: context]

      --budget <CHARS>
          Page size in characters, 0 for no limit [config: budget]

      --all
          Use every project's sessions, not only those of the current directory

      --since <WHEN>
          Only sessions active since WHEN: a date (2026-10-14) or an age (30m, 6h, 2d, 1w, 3mo)

      --until <WHEN>
          Only sessions active until WHEN: a date (whole day included) or an age

      --db <FILE>
          Database with the index, the transcript archive and the settings
          
          [env: CLAUDEGREP_DB=[ROOT]/db.sqlite]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
